@1 = ~Meeting with Shandalar~
@2 = ~Shandalar has asked you to meet him at his ship, just beyond the ridge east of the village.~
@6 = ~Flying Ship of Halruaa~
@7 = ~I need to search the forest where Shandalar's ship first crashed. A silver control rod essential to restoring the flying ship is believed to be somewhere among the wreckage.~

// CotSC localisation batch 7: independent I_C_T / I_C_T3 dialogue; existing entries unchanged.
@8 = ~Oh, what's that shiny thing in the jar...?~
@9 = ~No! Don't—~
@10 = ~Aw! It bit me!~
@11 = ~...touch that. You're lucky you didn't touch the larger jar next to it. You'd be losing a few fingers.~
@12 = ~Whoa. Puffguts used to read me stories about them when I was younger. I always wanted to see Halruaa and its fascinating flying ships. Honestly, I never put much faith in those stories as a child, but to see one with my own eyes...?~
@13 = ~Nothing spectacular. To think the Halruaans regard us Thayan mages as uppish renegades. Your inventions aren't nearly as extravagant as you'd like us to believe, and I see no brilliance whatsoever in this futile striving to draw attention to one's own splendour. (Although, I must admit, the craftsmanship and style are oddly peculiar and riveting.)~
@14 = ~Had you given me some time, I could conceive of a similar invention that would surpass the excellence of this ship. Of that, I have no doubt.~
